  "pages": [
    {
      "page_number": 1,
      "panels": [
        {
          "panel_number": 2,
          "texts": [
            {
              "kind": "caption",
              "text": "I sought the landlord for a room, and being told the house was full, I consented—if the harpooneer were not decidedly objectionable—to share a blanket rather than wander further on so bitter a night.",
              "caption_zone": "bottom_center"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "speaker": "Peter Coffin",
              "text": "You haint no objections to sharing a harpooneer’s blanket?",
              "balloon_zone": "top_right",
              "speaker_region": "right",
              "source_evidence": "“you haint no objections to sharing a harpooneer’s blanket, have ye?”"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "speaker": "Ishmael",
              "text": "If he’s decent, I’ll take half a blanket.",
              "balloon_zone": "bottom_left",
              "speaker_region": "left",
              "source_evidence": "“I would put up with the half of any decent man’s blanket.”"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_number": 2,
      "panels": [
        {
          "panel_number": 3,
          "texts": [
            {
              "kind": "caption",
              "text": "I changed my mind about that harpooneer, chose the bench, and soon learned that knots, a foot too short, and the meeting draughts would never do—while the landlord kept chuckling that the fellow was out ‘selling his head.’",
              "caption_zone": "top_right"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "speaker": "Ishmael",
              "text": "I shan’t sleep with him. I’ll try the bench here.",
              "balloon_zone": "top_left",
              "speaker_region": "left",
              "source_evidence": "“I shan’t sleep with him. I’ll try the bench here.”"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "speaker": "Peter Coffin",
              "text": "Wait a bit—I'll make ye snug enough.",
              "balloon_zone": "bottom_right",
              "speaker_region": "right",
              "source_evidence": "“wait a bit, Skrimshander… I’ll make ye snug enough.”"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_number": 4,
      "panels": [
        {
          "panel_number": 5,
          "texts": [
            {
              "kind": "caption",
              "text": "Seeing it was Sunday and he’d come to anchor elsewhere, I let the landlord lead me to the prodigious bed; I eyed the room and the harpooneer’s outlandish gear, then turned in.",
              "caption_zone": "top_center"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "speaker": "Peter Coffin",
              "text": "There; make yourself comfortable now, and good night to ye.",
              "balloon_zone": "bottom_right",
              "speaker_region": "right",
              "source_evidence": "“There… make yourself comfortable now, and good night to ye.”"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_number": 5,
      "panels": [
        {
          "panel_number": 7,
          "texts": [
            {
              "kind": "caption",
              "text": "Then, tomahawk-pipe between his teeth, he sprang into bed with me; I sang out, and the landlord burst in with a light to swear the harpooneer, Queequeg, wouldn’t harm a hair of my head.",
              "caption_zone": "top_right"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "speaker": "Ishmael",
              "text": "Landlord! Watch! Coffin! Angels! save me!",
              "balloon_zone": "bottom_left",
              "speaker_region": "left",
              "source_evidence": "“Landlord! Watch! Coffin! Angels! save me!”"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "speaker": "Queequeg",
              "text": "Who-e debel you? You no speak-e—dam-me, I kill-e.",
              "balloon_zone": "bottom_center",
              "speaker_region": "center",
              "source_evidence": "“Who-e debel you?—you no speak-e, dam-me, I kill-e.”"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "speaker": "Peter Coffin",
              "text": "Don't be afraid—Queequeg won't harm a hair of your head.",
              "balloon_zone": "bottom_right",
              "speaker_region": "right",
              "source_evidence": "“Queequeg here wouldn’t harm a hair of your head.”"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "panel_number": 8,
          "texts": [
            {
              "kind": "caption",
              "text": "Better sleep with a sober cannibal than a drunken Christian, thought I; he stashed the tomahawk-pipe, I turned in again, and never slept better in my life.",
              "caption_zone": "bottom_center"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "speaker": "Ishmael",
              "text": "Tell him to stash his tomahawk and stop smoking.",
              "balloon_zone": "top_left",
              "speaker_region": "left",
              "source_evidence": "“tell him to stash his tomahawk… tell him to stop smoking…”"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "speaker": "Queequeg",
              "text": "Me sabbee plenty.",
              "balloon_zone": "top_right",
              "speaker_region": "right",
              "source_evidence": "“Me sabbee plenty”"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_number": 6,
      "panels": [
        {
          "panel_number": 1,
          "texts": [
            {
              "kind": "caption",
              "text": "I woke at daylight to find Queequeg’s tattooed arm thrown over me, so blended with the patchwork counterpane that only its weight told me he was hugging me.",
              "caption_zone": "top_left"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "speaker": "Ishmael",
              "text": "Queequeg!",
              "balloon_zone": "bottom_left",
              "speaker_region": "left",
              "source_evidence": "“I now strove to rouse him—‘Queequeg!’—but his only answer was a snore.”"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "panel_number": 2,
          "texts": [
            {
              "kind": "caption",
              "text": "I tried to free myself and rouse him, rolled, felt a slight scratch, and, throwing aside the counterpane, I saw his tomahawk-pipe lying by his side.",
              "caption_zone": "bottom_left"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "speaker": "Ishmael",
              "text": "In the name of goodness, Queequeg—wake!",
              "balloon_zone": "top_left",
              "speaker_region": "left",
              "source_evidence": "“Queequeg!—in the name of goodness, Queequeg, wake!”"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
